[Mod] Rats Pop-Out Windows 1.1: window handling for Sea Power, on one monitor or two

A while ago I posted a small mod that moves Sea Power's windows to a second monitor. Since then it grew into the window handling I always missed in this game. The windows now stay where you put them, you can maximize, snap and dim them, and the Encyclopedia finally has a search that finds things. Most of it works with a single monitor too.

[b]Windows[/b]
[list]
[*]Position and size are remembered, also after a restart
[*]Double-click a title bar to maximize, double-click again to restore
[*]Windows snap to the screen edges and to each other, with wide resize corners
[*]A look button per window: opacity, scale, text outline, keep it below or above the others
[*]A gear button with all settings, in the game's nine languages
[/list]

[b]Encyclopedia[/b]
[list]
[*]Search finds unit ids and words from the description, "Type 072" finds the Yukan class
[*]Loadout variants get real names like "Long-Hull [Early]" instead of bare years
[*]A click on a class opens its earliest variant
[*]"Armed only", and the country list only shows countries that still have units for your search
[*]The unit list can be made wider or hidden, and remembers your country and search
[/list]

[b]In missions and campaigns[/b]
[list]
[*]Unit Status has a Reference tab with the unit's data and loadouts
[*]Right-click the flag or name in the unit panel for the unit's menu, also for contacts
[*]The time panel can be dragged anywhere
[*]Task Force Builder lists loadouts oldest first, plus a "Strict loadouts" option for new campaigns
[/list]

[b]Second monitor (as before)[/b]
[list]
[*]One click on the new title bar button moves a window to your second monitor and back
[*]Over there only the windows show, they snap together and are remembered for the next mission
[/list]

[b]Game version[/b] Made for Sea Power 0.8.7. The 3D globe beta is not supported yet, that comes later.

Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3380210757]Anchor Chain[/url].

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3826396311]Workshop page[/url] · [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerPopOut]Source code (MIT)[/url]

If something looks off on your setup, tell me and attach BepInEx\LogOutput.log. Every feature has its own switch in the gear panel, so you can turn off whatever you don't like.
